Andrew Kerr <andykerr@SPAMGUARD.blueyonder.co.uk> wrote:
>A couple of YANIs for enforcing late game weapon type differentiation:
>
>*	Luck added to to-hit total logarithmically, not linearly, or even 
>	not added at all.

My luck table would look like this for positive luck:

13-14 +4
9-12  +3
5-8   +2
1-4   +1

Zero luck would give no bonus; negative luck would still give a penalty
equal to the negative luck total.

>*	Experience levels added to-to hit total logarithmically.

I like "Experience levels added to melee and ranged to-hit totals in
different ways based on class."  Something like:

Valkyrie, Barbarian: +1/level to melee, +.75/level to ranged
Samurai, Caveman: +.9/level to both
Knight, Monk: +.9/level to melee, +.6/level to ranged
Rangers: +.75/level to melee, +1/level to ranged
Rogues: +.75/level to both
Priests: +.75/level to melee, +.5/level to ranged
Archeologists: +.5/level to both
Healers, Tourists, Wizards: +.3/level to both

(Obviously the values would need extensive playtesting.)
